# 09b round-5 distinguishing ablations of clean payload C5

Payload C5: e0660effc729b968c528943220d9ba6fbc561c18.
Each ablation changes exactly one behaviour in a detached worktree at C5, runs
packages/kernel/tests/*.test.ts against it, and is reverted before the next.
An ablation is REJECTED when named packet cases fail; that is what makes those cases
distinguishing rather than merely green.

Method notes for two round-5 corrections: the caller-vs-snapshot ablation calls unmodified
JCS directly on the caller's object (bypassing both capture and the safe clone), because the
safe clone itself reads own descriptors and would otherwise mask the ordinary-read difference
the ablation is meant to remove; the "01" ablation drops the String(numeric)===name check as
well as widening the regex, because the regex alone still rejects "01" via that second check.
The LIMIT-01 ablation's 115-test count is the old code aborting values.test.ts on the 20M
traversal (native stack/OOM after ~19s), which itself proves the unbounded path.

